.TH QDROPD 1 "qdrop 0.0.1" "qdrop" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
qdropd \- the qdrop daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B qdropd
[\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-\-port\fR \fIPORT\fR] [\fB\-\-check\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B qdropd
is the long\-running background service. It advertises and browses
.I _qdrop._tcp
over mDNS, holds one mutually\-authenticated TLS\ 1.3 connection per paired
peer, and runs clipboard sync and file transfer. Trust is established once with
.BR "qdrop pair" (1).
.PP
It logs to standard error and exits cleanly on
.B SIGTERM
or
.BR "Ctrl\-C" .
A service manager (see
.BR launchd (8)
or
.BR systemd.user (5))
keeps it running and restarts it on crash.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Debug\-level logging. Overridden by the
.B RUST_LOG
environment variable.
.TP
.BR \-\-port " " \fIPORT\fR
Override the listen port from
.IR config.toml .
.TP
.B \-\-check
Load and validate configuration, log the plan, and exit without binding
anything.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/qdrop/config.toml
Daemon configuration (all keys optional).
.TP
.I ~/.config/qdrop/peers.toml
Paired\-device registry, written by
.BR "qdrop pair" (1).
.TP
.I ~/.config/qdrop/identity.pem
Long\-term Ed25519 identity key (mode 0600).
.TP
.I ~/.config/qdrop/state.json
Live connection status, read by
.BR "qdrop status" (1).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR qdrop (1)
